+      <strong>HSC mark</strong> is the number on your results notice (out of 100, or 50 for 1-unit Extension) — the average of your moderated assessment mark and your exam mark, aligned to bands. It is <em>not</em> your raw exam mark; raw marks are never published and are usually much lower.
+      <strong>Contribution</strong> is what <em>one course</em> is worth toward your ATAR, on an ATAR-like scale. A course contributing 95 is pulling its weight for a 95 ATAR. Your actual ATAR comes from the best 10 units together, so courses trade off — one at 92 can be carried by one at 98.</span>
